{# COMING UP on the roads out of Largs (27 Nov 2026, Ian: "people are
   interested in more than just now", and it "needs to be automated, not a
   manual process").

   Everything here is worked out by scripts/fetch-data.mjs (buildAhead)
   from the Scottish Road Works Register's nightly file: works on the A78
   from Greenock to Ardrossan, the Haylie Brae road (A760) and the A737,
   that hold up traffic and are registered to start within three months.
   Nobody types any of it. The same job filed several times is one row.

   The words are the register's own, shorthand expanded and nothing more:
   this list does not rewrite what a works promoter filed. The register
   gives dates and not hours, and says how firm a booking is; both are
   said on the page. `aheadNow` drops a row on the day after it starts.

   LENGTH. Three months of three roads was twenty-seven rows on the first
   day, seven phone screens above the Largs list. So each road shows its
   road closures and convoy working, and the next two of anything else;
   the remainder open under one line (`aheadSplit`), no script needed.

   A full closure whose nights and hours matter (A78, November 2026) is
   still a hand-kept notice in planned.json, from the operator's own
   published hours; the register cannot say that much. #}
{% macro aheadRow(w) %}
  <article class="work-row">
    <span class="chip {% if w.what == "Road closure" %}active{% else %}planned{% endif %}">{{ w.from | dom }} {{ w.from | monthShort }}</span>
    <div class="work-main">
      <h4>{{ w.what }} — {{ w.title }}</h4>
      {% if w.text and (w.text | lower) != (w.where | lower) %}<p class="work-gloss">{{ w.text }}</p>{% endif %}
      <p class="meta">
        {%- if w.promoter %}{{ w.promoter }} · {% endif -%}
        {%- if w.from == w.until %}on {{ w.from | dom }} {{ w.from | monthShort }}{% if w.fromYear %} {{ w.fromYear }}{% endif %}
        {%- else %}{{ w.from | dom }} {{ w.from | monthShort }} to {{ w.until | dom }} {{ w.until | monthShort }}{% if w.untilYear %} {{ w.untilYear }}{% endif %}{% endif -%}
        {%- if w.status %} · {{ w.status }}{% endif -%}
        {%- if w.more %} · filed for {{ w.more + 1 }} places{% endif -%}
        {%- if w.busText %} · may affect buses {{ w.busText }}{% endif -%}
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
{% endmacro %}
{% set ahead = today.roadworks.ahead %}
{% if today.roadworks.ok and ahead %}
{% set aheadItems = ahead.items | aheadNow %}
<section class="coming-up" id="coming-up" aria-labelledby="coming-up-h">
  <h2 id="coming-up-h">Coming up on the roads out of Largs</h2>
  <p class="page-intro">Works registered to start in the next three months on
  the A78, the Haylie Brae road (A760) and the A737, from the Scottish Road
  Works Register, each described in the words it was filed in. The register
  gives dates, not hours, and a planned date can move. <strong>Red</strong>
  is a road closure; amber is everything else.</p>
  {% for g in ahead.groups %}
  {% set groupRows = aheadItems | aheadInGroup(g.key) %}
  <h3 class="coming-up-group">{{ g.label }} · {{ g.roads }}</h3>
  {% if groupRows | length == 0 %}<p class="note coming-up-none">Nothing registered to start in the next three months.</p>{% endif %}
  {% set split = groupRows | aheadSplit %}
  {% for w in split.lead %}{{ aheadRow(w) }}{% endfor %}
  {% if split.rest | length %}
  <details class="coming-up-more">
    <summary>{{ split.rest | length }} more on this road: lights, lane closures and the like</summary>
    {% for w in split.rest %}{{ aheadRow(w) }}{% endfor %}
  </details>
  {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
  <p class="note">Register data to {{ today.roadworks.dataDate | dom }} {{ today.roadworks.dataDate | monthShort }} · refreshed overnight · “advance planning” and “proposed” are the register’s own words for a booking that is not yet confirmed.</p>
</section>
{% endif %}
